hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"119","""I have not seen anything more beautiful than Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace). The sun seemed to shine in his face. Nor have I seen anyone more rapid in his gait than Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace). The earth seemed to be folded up for him. We must strenuously exert ourselves, while he is not subject to any stress."""","" on the authority of her paternal uncle; 'While I was walking in Medina"","" someone behind me said: ‘Raise your loincloth"","" for that is more pious and conducive to longer wear.’ Lo and behold"","" he was Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace)'"","" so I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"","" it is simply a black garment with white stripes!’ He said: ‘Do you not have an example in me?’ so I looked and noticed that his loincloth was to half his shins'.”"""""
"120","\'Uthman ibn 'Affan used to wear a loincloth reaching the middle parts of his shins"","" and he said: 'In this manner was the loincloth of my Companion'"","" meaning the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace).”"""""
"121","\Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) took hold of the calf of my leg or his leg"","" and he said: 'This is the position of the loincloth"","" and if you object"","" then somewhat lower down"","" but if you object"","" the loincloth has no right to the ankles'.”"""""
